\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Polish audit \'97 what stands between minimark and "finished"\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Written 4 September 2026, against 
\f2\fs26 tabs
\f1\fs24  at 
\f2\fs26 ef72d8a
\f1\fs24  plus the uncommitted reveal work. Read this before picking up polish work; it is ordered by what it costs a person, not by what it costs to fix.\
Ground truth first, because it changes how the list should be read: 
\f2\fs26 ./build.sh
\f1\fs24  produces a clean universal binary, 
\f2\fs26 codesign --verify
\f1\fs24  passes, and all eight test suites are green (34 focus assertions, 13 encoding assertions, and the rest). 
\f0\b Nothing below is breakage.
\f1\b0  It is the gap between an app that works and an app that nobody has to be forgiving about.\
Everything here was verified against the source or against the running app, not inferred from the roadmap.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
