\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 Tier 1 \'97 costs someone their work, or their trust\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 1. An untitled document is never written anywhere\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs26 \cf0 scheduleAutosave
\f1\fs24  (
\f2\fs26 minimark.swift:1914
\f1\fs24 ) returns early unless 
\f3\i some
\f1\i0  tab has a URL, and 
\f2\fs26 runAutosave
\f1\fs24  writes only 
\f2\fs26 tab.dirty && tab.url != nil
\f1\fs24 . Session restore drops untitled tabs because there is nowhere to put their text. So everything typed before the first 
\f4 \uc0\u8984 
\f1 S lives in one WKWebView's memory and nowhere else.\
A normal quit asks. A crash, a force-quit, a power cut, a WebKit process crash: all silent, all total. Tabs made this worse rather than better, because several untitled documents at once is now one 
\f4 \uc0\u8984 
\f1 T away.\
The fix is the one the roadmap already names. Write untitled buffers to 
\f2\fs26 ~/Library/Application Support/minimark/unsaved/
\f1\fs24  on the same 1s debounce, and offer them back at launch. It closes the session-restore hole in the same move.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 2. Autosave fails silently, and the status bar says everything is fine\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs26 \cf0 write(text, to: url, silent: true)
\f1\fs24  with 
\f2\fs26 guard \'85 else \{ return \}
\f1\fs24 . A read-only volume, a full disk, an ejected drive, a permissions change: the file stops being saved and 
\f3\i nothing on screen changes
\f1\i0 . Worse, 
\f2\fs26 updateSaved
\f1\fs24  keeps showing "saved 4m ago" from the last successful write, which reads as reassurance.\
The silence was the right call, since the old behaviour was an alert a second. The counting is what was never finished. Count consecutive failures per tab, and on the third say so once, in the status bar rather than in a sheet.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 3. Rename can make the file disappear\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs26 \cf0 renameDocument
\f1\fs24  (
\f2\fs26 :1880
\f1\fs24 ) strips 
\f2\fs26 /
\f1\fs24  and 
\f2\fs26 :
\f1\fs24  and trims whitespace. It does not strip a leading dot. Rename to 
\f2\fs26 .notes
\f1\fs24  and the file is still there and Finder will never show it again. One line, and the cheapest fix on this list.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 4. iCloud, Dropbox and git worktrees will produce conflicts\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Nothing uses 
\f2\fs26 NSFileCoordinator
\f1\fs24  or 
\f2\fs26 NSFilePresenter
\f1\fs24 . A 2-second mtime poll (
\f2\fs26 kWatchInterval
\f1\fs24 ) races a 1-second autosave (
\f2\fs26 kAutosaveDelay
\f1\fs24 ). For a markdown editor the likely audience keeps its notes in exactly those places, so this is not an edge case. It is the default deployment.\
Bigger than the three above and worth scheduling on its own.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
