\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 6. Right-click gives a browser menu, including Inspect Element\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 There is no 
\f2\fs26 WKUIDelegate
\f1\fs24  context-menu customisation anywhere in the shell, and 
\f2\fs26 developerExtrasEnabled
\f1\fs24  (
\f2\fs26 :959
\f1\fs24 ) and 
\f2\fs26 isInspectable
\f1\fs24  (
\f2\fs26 :976
\f1\fs24 ) are both unconditionally true. So right-clicking a word in a writing app offers Reload, Services and Inspect Element.\
This is the loudest "there is a web view under here" tell in the product. A curated menu (Cut, Copy, Paste, Look Up, spelling suggestions, and the formatting actions already in the bubble) would do more for the feel of the app than any animation in it. Wrap the two dev-tools flags in 
\f2\fs26 #if DEBUG
\f1\fs24  at the same time.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 7. minimark cannot become the default markdown app\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs26 \cf0 LSHandlerRank
\f1\fs24  is 
\f2\fs26 Alternate
\f1\fs24  for both document types in 
\f2\fs26 Info.plist
\f1\fs24 . It should be 
\f2\fs26 Owner
\f1\fs24  for markdown and stay 
\f2\fs26 Alternate
\f1\fs24  for plain text. Until it is, "Change All\'85" in Finder does not reliably stick, and double-clicking a 
\f2\fs26 .md
\f1\fs24  file opens somebody else's editor.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 8. Images arrive with no alt text\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs26 \cf0 insertImages
\f1\fs24  writes 
\f2\fs26 ![](name)
\f1\fs24  and moves on. Nothing prompts, and the writer never thinks about it again, so every exported HTML page and every PDF ends up with unlabelled images. 
\f2\fs26 insertLink
\f1\fs24  already does the right thing by selecting the 
\f2\fs26 label
\f1\fs24  placeholder so it can be typed straight over. Images should do the same with 
\f2\fs26 alt
\f1\fs24 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 9. The heading outline is invisible until you happen to hover it\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs26 \cf0 #scrub \{ opacity: 0 \}
\f1\fs24  with 
\f2\fs26 #scrub.has:hover \{ opacity: 1 \}
\f1\fs24 . It is a good feature that essentially nobody will find, because finding it means moving the pointer into a 30px strip at the right edge for no reason. A faint resting state once a document has headings, or a brief appearance while scrolling, would earn back what it costs.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 10. A wikilink to a file that does not exist looks exactly like one that does\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Known and deliberately left, because telling them apart means a round trip per link. Worth revisiting with one batched round trip per render instead.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

